Maybe I'm missing the point, but why not just start the game in
explore mode (slashem -X)? This way you start with a wand of wishing.
Ok, I know it's not the same thing - if you win in explore mode your
game will not go to the score list. But if you ascend with an easyness
patch applied it will be different from ascending with a normal game
anyways (at least one can not brag so much here in r.g.r.n if he
ascend slash'em in easy mode :-)

Note that I'm not saying your idea is bad... just that it seems for me
that if one is going to play slash'em in an easier mode, 'just for the
fun', I think it's better just playing the explore mode. This way you
can choose your 'easyness level' too (your wizard can wish for a
spellbook of magic missile or any other item he wants to start the
game with).

The option for a more difficult game, OTOH, is a more interesting
idea... but even for this you can just drop some of the things at your
starting inventory and choose not to use them, to make the game more
difficult. Of course, this do not help with already known spells, and
that's the point where a difficult setting could be desirable.

Just my 2 zorkmids...

